{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"nonmystic-sterilised-gemsbok","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\nMeasured while answering 'how do we safely reduce the 1.02 GiB packed .git'. The tickets and their sidecars are NOT the problem. The Jira reconciler's bridge state is.\n\n## Measured pack composition (pack-b2b621b8, 212,856 objects)\n\n| content | packed |\n|---|---|\n| `.bridge_state/bindings.json` | **739.8 MB** (3,009 blobs, avg 252 KB) |\n| `.bridge_state/prev_snapshot.json` | **202.7 MB** (5,151 blobs, avg 40 KB) |\n| ALL real ticket events (SNAPSHOT/COMMENT/EDIT/CREATE/STATUS/LINK/...) | ~14 MB |\n| REVIEW_RESULT sidecars | 24.5 MB |\n| code + everything else | 25.9 MB |\n\nBridge state is **942.5 MB of a 1.03 GiB pack (91%)**. Working-tree sizes: `bindings.json` 17 MB, `prev_snapshot.json` 26 MB - two large single files rewritten in full on every reconcile.\n\n## Root cause of the churn (measured on two consecutive revisions)\n\nBetween consecutive writes the file grows only **+2,470 bytes**, and only **1,229 added / 1,166 deleted lines out of 526,487 (0.45%)**. But of those ~2,395 changed lines, **2,290 are `baseline_advanced_at` timestamp updates** - 96%% of the churn. The remaining ~69 lines are real change (`type`, `text`, `last_get_pass`).\n\nIn one file version there are 1,507 `baseline_advanced_at` occurrences with 230 distinct values - but **1,145 of them carry the SAME value**, bumped together on each pass. It is one logical fact (this pass advanced the baseline at time T) physically duplicated across ~1,145 binding entries.\n\nThe field is only 0.4%% of the file's bytes, but the edits are SCATTERED across all 18 MB, so every reconcile produces a delta with ~1,145 separate change regions. That is what defeats delta compression and yields 252 KB packed per version.\n\n## Why the obvious remedies do not work\n\n- **Aggressive repack will not help materially.** The blobs are ALREADY deltified: 8,157 of 8,165 bridge-state blobs have delta depth > 0 (avg depth 13.9) and still occupy 940.5 MB. Only 8 blobs (1.9 MB) are non-deltified. There is essentially no delta headroom left.\n- **`git gc`** reclaims only the 3 stray `tmp_pack_*` files (3.67 MiB) and consolidates 14 packs. Free, but small.\n- **History rewrite** would reclaim the most but is unsafe: `tickets` is the shared source of truth and rewriting it breaks every clone.\n\n## Fix direction (stops the bleeding; safe, no history rewrite)\n\nStop rewriting a per-binding field that is really one global fact:\n1. Hoist `baseline_advanced_at` to a single top-level value (per pass), leaving per-binding entries untouched when nothing about that binding changed; or\n2. only update a binding's `baseline_advanced_at` when that binding actually changed.\n\nEither collapses per-reconcile churn from ~2,395 changed lines to ~69, which should cut new-version delta cost by roughly 97%%.\n\nWorth considering alongside: whether `prev_snapshot.json` (26 MB, 5,151 versions, 202 MB packed) needs to be versioned at all, or is a derived cache that could live outside git.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A reconcile pass that changes N bindings produces a bindings.json diff proportional to N, not to the total binding count.\n- [ ] Measured: consecutive-revision changed-line count drops from ~2,395 to the order of the number of genuinely-changed bindings.\n- [ ] A decision is recorded on whether `prev_snapshot.json` must be committed at all.\n- [ ] No change to reconciler correctness: binding resolution and baseline semantics are unchanged (covered by existing reconciler tests).","id":"7f6c-df12-e3dc-4691","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["reconciler","git","repo-size","performance"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Jira bridge state is 91% of the git pack: a per-binding timestamp is rewritten on every reconcile"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785350110957617001,"uuid":"0c894e86-4be7-4606-9df3-48df5cd6837a"}